  showLeadForm={true}
  publishDate="2026-03-28"
  updateDate="2026-09-05"
>

<p>A professional website audit connects observed problems to an implementation plan. AuditWeb reviews the agreed pages and systems, records evidence and recommends a sequence of fixes.</p>
<p>Choose a focused review or a broader assessment. Confirm the page sample, available data, deliverables and delivery date before work begins.</p>

<h2 id="whats-included-in-our-audit">What's Included in Our Audit</h2>
<p>The agreed scope determines the checks. A basic review focuses on essential technical and on-page issues. A comprehensive review adds content, competitive context and user experience. The audit checklist provides a starting framework; findings depend on the actual evidence.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Technical SEO:</strong> crawl access, response codes, canonical signals, internal links and indexing evidence where Search Console access is available.</li>
<li><strong>On-page and content:</strong> titles, descriptions, heading structure, search intent and content gaps.</li>
<li><strong>Performance and experience:</strong> loading behaviour, key page templates, mobile layouts and agreed visitor journeys.</li>
<li><strong>Security checks:</strong> agreed public configuration checks such as HTTPS and response headers. This does not constitute penetration testing or a security certification.</li>
</ul>
<p>Use the <a href="/website-audit-checklist/">website audit checklist</a> to explore the areas available for review.</p>

<h2 id="our-audit-process">Our Audit Process</h2>
<p>The review moves from a defined question to evidence and a practical handoff.</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Agree the scope.</strong> Identify the website, business question, priority pages and available data. Confirm deliverables and timing.</li>
<li><strong>Collect evidence.</strong> Review the agreed pages and systems. Record observations, affected URLs and any access limitations.</li>
<li><strong>Prioritise findings.</strong> Separate confirmed problems from issues needing investigation. Assess impact, effort and dependencies.</li>
<li><strong>Deliver the action plan.</strong> Document recommended changes and the checks needed to verify them. Agree any walkthrough or follow-up support in the scope.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="sample-deliverables">Sample Deliverables</h2>
<p>A useful report gives the person implementing a fix enough evidence to reproduce the problem and check the result.</p>
<ul><li>Executive summary of the observed problems and recommended first actions.</li><li>Findings with affected pages, evidence and reproduction steps.</li><li>Recommended fixes with priorities, dependencies and limitations.</li><li>Implementation plan with verification criteria.</li></ul>
<p>Read our <a href="/case-studies/auditweb-self-audit/">documented self-audit</a> for an actual owned-site example. It does not claim a client outcome or traffic uplift.</p>
<p>The <a href="/resources/agency-audit-toolkit/">editable agency toolkit</a> shows the report fields and implementation tracker.</p>

<h2 id="who-its-for">Who It's For</h2>
<p>Professional review suits website owners, marketing teams and agencies that need help investigating a problem or deciding what to fix first.</p>
<ul><li>Business owners who need a clear explanation of a website issue.</li><li>Marketing teams preparing changes to important search or conversion pages.</li><li>Agencies seeking additional review capacity for an agreed client scope.</li><li>Teams planning a migration or reviewing a recent release.</li></ul>

<h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2>
<p>Basic audits start at $297. Comprehensive audits start at $997. Prices below are in USD. Confirm the final scope and terms before commissioning work.</p>
<div class="service-pricing">
<section><h3>Basic · $297</h3><p>Essential technical, on-page and mobile checks with a prioritised report. Suitable for a focused review of a smaller site.</p></section>
<section><h3>Comprehensive · $997</h3><p>Broader technical, content, competitive and experience review with an implementation plan. Agree the page sample and walkthrough in advance.</p></section>
<section><h3>Custom scope</h3><p>Large sites, migrations, multiple languages and complex architectures need a tailored assessment and quote.</p></section>
</div>
<p>Read the <a href="/website-audit-services/cost/">audit cost guide</a> for the factors that affect scope and pricing.</p>

<h2 id="our-guarantee">Scope and Terms Before Work Begins</h2>
<p>Confirm the scope, price, delivery date, access requirements and any cancellation or refund terms in writing before commissioning an audit. Ranking positions and revenue changes are not guaranteed.</p>
<p>The audit covers investigation and recommendations. Implementation and ongoing monitoring require a separately agreed scope.</p>

<h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
<h3>How long does the audit take?</h3><p>Timing depends on site size, available data and review depth. Agree a delivery date after scoping the work.</p>
<h3>What access do you need?</h3><p>Public pages can be reviewed without an account. Search Console and analytics access can provide additional evidence. Agree read-only access where appropriate; do not send passwords through the enquiry form.</p>
<h3>Will you implement the fixes?</h3><p>Implementation is a separate engagement. The report includes recommended changes and verification criteria.</p>
<h3>How is this different from the free checker?</h3><p>The free checker inspects pasted HTML in your browser. A professional audit investigates the agreed site scope and adds interpretation, priorities and implementation guidance.</p>
<h3>Do you work with agencies?</h3><p>Agency work can be scoped around client requirements, reporting format and review capacity. Confirm branding and delivery arrangements before work starts.</p>
<h3>Can I see an example first?</h3><p>Yes. The documented self-audit shows actual findings from AuditWeb. The downloadable toolkit contains blank templates you can inspect and reuse.</p>
</ContentLayout>
